meta {
  name: Submit Write Request
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/write-requests/{{writeRequestId}}/submit
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

docs {
  Turn a saved DRAFT into a live request: it enters the approval queue, or — on a DIRECT-policy environment — runs immediately as the caller. 409s on any other status.

  409 if the draft's connection changed since it was saved (host, env, … — see Approve) — revise it to bind it to the current connection; also 409 if the connection is edited while the request is being validated. Nothing runs either way.

  Whoever submits becomes the request's requester, so the approve route's self-approval block covers them: you cannot submit a draft and then approve it yourself.

  503 `CONNECTION_FAILED` when a direct run can't reach the database before sending anything: nothing ran, the request is back in DRAFT, and the body carries it as `request`. Audited as `WRITE_EXECUTE_ERROR`.

  Requires **write** capability on the request's environment and a valid Bearer JWT ({{token}}).
  Requires **write mode** to be enabled.

  Object changes: 409 `{ code: "OBJECT_CHANGED" }` when the object's deployed definition no longer matches the snapshot taken at submit — nothing runs and the request is unchanged; revise it to re-base.
}
